From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ampheck <support@ampheck.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: rk808: match the RK8xx clkout platform device names

The RK808 MFD creates platform devices named rk805-clkout, rk808-clkout,
rk816-clkout, rk817-clkout and rk818-clkout.  The clock driver's ID table
uses the -clk suffix instead, so none of those devices bind and the PMIC
never registers its clock provider.  Consumers of the RK809 32 kHz clock,
such as the AP6256 SDIO power sequence, then defer forever.

Match the actual MFD device names so the clock provider is registered.

Signed-off-by: Ampheck <support@ampheck.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/clk-rk808.c b/drivers/clk/clk-rk808.c
index 820dc2b11..bccf6be73 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/clk-rk808.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk-rk808.c
@@ -195,11 +195,11 @@ static int rk808_clkout_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 }
 
 static const struct platform_device_id rk8xx_clk_id_table[] = {
-	{ "rk805-clk", 0 },
-	{ "rk809-clk", 0 },
-	{ "rk816-clk", 0 },
-	{ "rk817-clk", 0 },
-	{ "rk818-clk", 0 },
+	{ "rk805-clkout", 0 },
+	{ "rk808-clkout", 0 },
+	{ "rk816-clkout", 0 },
+	{ "rk817-clkout", 0 },
+	{ "rk818-clkout", 0 },
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(platform, rk8xx_clk_id_table);
-- 
